 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Keep it in a bag with ice packs, or in the fridge, or in the freezer. A cooler is the slowest. Blocks are a lot cheaper, and you can make them at home. Ice cubes melt faster. Pack the cold stuff in first, then fill the space with dry stuff so the cold doesn't leak out. Then label the cold stuff on the outside, so he sees it. And put the drinks in a cooler with its own ice. Yes, let it warm up a bit before feeding it. It tastes better, and it digests better.",
